<figure class="chapter-visual ks-map">
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创静态示意：相互作用体系与 Kohn–Sham 辅助体系</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original static diagram: interacting and Kohn–Sham auxiliary systems</span>
  </figcaption>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 900 430" role="img" aria-labelledby="ks-map-title ks-map-desc">
    <title id="ks-map-title">Interacting system and Kohn–Sham auxiliary system connected by the same ground-state density</title>
    <desc id="ks-map-desc">The interacting many-body Hamiltonian and a local noninteracting Kohn–Sham Hamiltonian have different wavefunctions and interactions but are constrained to reproduce the same ground-state density.</desc>

    <rect x="35" y="70" width="330" height="235" rx="24" class="ks-map__system ks-map__system--interacting" />
    <text x="200" y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="ks-map__heading">真实相互作用体系</text>
    <text x="200" y="139" text-anchor="middle" lang="en">interacting many-body system</text>
    <text x="200" y="185" text-anchor="middle">H = T + W + Vext</text>
    <text x="200" y="221" text-anchor="middle">多体态 Ψ₀</text>
    <text x="200" y="252" text-anchor="middle" lang="en">correlated many-body state</text>
    <text x="200" y="285" text-anchor="middle">W ≠ 0</text>

    <rect x="535" y="70" width="330" height="235" rx="24" class="ks-map__system ks-map__system--auxiliary" />
    <text x="700" y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="ks-map__heading">辅助非相互作用体系</text>
    <text x="700" y="139" text-anchor="middle" lang="en">Kohn–Sham auxiliary system</text>
    <text x="700" y="185" text-anchor="middle">hKS = −∇²/2 + vKS</text>
    <text x="700" y="221" text-anchor="middle">轨道集合 {φᵢ}</text>
    <text x="700" y="252" text-anchor="middle" lang="en">single-particle orbitals</text>
    <text x="700" y="285" text-anchor="middle">Waux = 0</text>

    <path d="M 365 180 C 430 130 470 130 535 180" class="ks-map__arrow" marker-end="url(#ks-map-arrow)" />
    <path d="M 535 245 C 470 295 430 295 365 245" class="ks-map__arrow" marker-end="url(#ks-map-arrow)" />
    <text x="450" y="130" text-anchor="middle">同一基态密度</text>
    <text x="450" y="153" text-anchor="middle" lang="en">same ground-state density</text>
    <text x="450" y="326" text-anchor="middle">n₀(r)=Σᵢ fᵢ|φᵢ(r)|²</text>

    <rect x="245" y="345" width="410" height="60" rx="18" class="ks-map__functional" />
    <text x="450" y="371" text-anchor="middle">未知多体差额收集到 Exc[n]</text>
    <text x="450" y="394" text-anchor="middle" lang="en">the residual many-body contribution is assigned to Exc[n]</text>

    <defs>
      <marker id="ks-map-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" />
      </marker>
    </defs>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>学习目的：</strong>区分真实体系与辅助体系的 Hamiltonian、态和相互作用，同时保留唯一的匹配条件——基态密度相同。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Learning purpose:</strong> distinguish the Hamiltonians, states, and interactions of the physical and auxiliary systems while preserving the sole matching condition: the same ground-state density.</p>
    <p><strong>输入与输出：</strong>输入是固定粒子数、真实外势、电子相互作用和一个假定存在的局域 Kohn–Sham 势；输出是两体系共享的密度。图中没有数值单位或可调参数。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Input and output:</strong> the inputs are fixed particle number, physical external potential, electron interaction, and an assumed local Kohn–Sham potential; the output is the shared density. The diagram has no numerical units or controls.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>两侧不得显示同一波函数；辅助侧相互作用必须为零；共同箭头只能标记密度约束，不能暗示 Kohn–Sham 轨道等于真实准粒子态。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the two sides must not share a wavefunction; the auxiliary interaction is zero; the common arrow labels only the density constraint and does not identify Kohn–Sham orbitals with quasiparticle states.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>这是结构关系图，不证明非相互作用 ground-state v-representability，也不构造 vKS。真实体系和辅助体系的激发谱通常不同。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> this structural diagram neither proves noninteracting ground-state v-representability nor constructs vKS. The excitation spectra of the two systems generally differ.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

